WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.475
This slide isolates one rule that explains many
NULL-related surprises WHERE keeps

00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:09.250
only TRUE The example creates three rows with
Boolean states true false

00:00:09.388 --> 00:00:14.725
and NULL then applies WHERE flag Only the true row
remains The

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.938
false row is removed as expected and the unknown row
is also

00:00:17.962 --> 00:00:22.325
removed because SQL cannot prove the condition true
This matters when a

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.662
nullable field such as consent is used in a filter
Decide whether

00:00:26.675 --> 00:00:31.838
unknown values should be excluded included for
review or treated separately Do

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:35.588
not let WHERE's default behavior make that policy
decision accidentally
